Just learnt class property name and method name are NOT Identifier in ECMA spec, it's called ClassElementName. Similar to the PropertyName in ObjectLiteral, which is NOT Identifier either.

Keywords cannot be Identifier, but can be ClassElementName and PropertyName.

```js
class A {
 let = 1;
 function = 2;
 static voi\u0064 = 3; // escaped void
 async *var() {}
}
```
The above are all valid. :)

### Changelog category (leave one):
- Improvement


### Changelog entry (a user-readable short description of the changes that goes to CHANGELOG.md):
Various improvements in the advanced dashboard. This closes #67697. This closes #63407. This closes #51129. This closes #61204.

The following changes are made:
- time is displayed in UTC;
- time is displayed in ISO 8601 (the previous format didn't even display seconds);
- ticks on the x-axis are aligned and selected by the UTC time (not to the local time);
- ticks on the x-axis will not overlap;
- day is displayed once for each day; repeating values for the same day will display only the time of day;
- the legend balloon will not overflow the chart's area; it will always display inside;
- the legend balloon will align numbers to the right;
- the legend color is changed;
- numbers on the y-axis will be formatted with decimal suffixes (K, M, G, T, P, and also μ);
- the padding of the chart on the left will be constant among charts so they are aligned better;
- fix invalid detection of empty result: in previous versions, it showed "Wrong data format of the query" instead of "Query returned empty result."
- when pressing on the mass edit button, the focus is set to the text editor;
- improve margins when there are many parameters;
- automatic field width of chart parameters;


